reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/CONCLUSIONS.md:19:Reconstruct identical saved candidate requests; interleave fresh no-score controls with true-score requests and a score-shuffled control, with fixed score representation and randomization, repeated draws, cache misses, and identical model, candidates and question content except score lines. Make each score's query origin explicit: multiple search queries may yield different scores. A shuffled control tests sensitivity to a number but needs care with singleton/equal-score cases and preserving query origin. A source-blind independent reader judges differing pairs and controls without seeing arm, score, or prior decision. Report wrong merges, missed repeats, incorrect revision classifications and group choices separately, all cases, with same-arm variability, cost and limitations; fixed-candidate comparisons do not prove forward-run performance. The fresh set has few or no revisions; use separately identified stored revision cases without presenting isolated pair results as product-path evidence. Freeze design, audit and preflight under repository rules before any paid send. A score can also encode context Jev did not directly receive (e.g. thesis wording or period), so improvement would not itself establish the mechanism.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/EXPERIMENT-DESIGN.md:16:| Crash or interruption | Journal dispatch with flush and fsync; on any interruption stop and inspect, with no automatic resume or re-send. A dispatch without completion is ambiguous. | Save identifiers, not wall-clock ordering |
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/EXPERIMENT-DESIGN.md:54:D381 selects the candidate with highest Jev same-statement probability; this experiment retains it. D379 seals old product; no frozen files or production config touched. AGENTS §7.1 historical rulers unchanged; repeat reference is exploratory, not new frozen gold. AGENTS §7.2 read raw answer against source. Current Jev model `jev-1.14.0`. Offline census reconstructs and verifies all 185 comparison requests and answers. Standing preflight run against v108 archive judged 243 extraction answers and 170 matching records, two matching records skipped, 12 extraction records dropped and 2 stored schema refusals; that script does not test the clean Jev score path. The latter needs its own replay and refusal controls before send.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/EXPERIMENT-DESIGN.md:58:Hypothesis: score information moves at least one relevant comparison and makes at least one source-backed decision better without a source-backed decision getting worse. Prediction: the clearly wrong X22 grouping becomes separate more often in T than C, while the selected accepted-repeat controls remain correctly grouped. We do not predict a perfect result. Predeclare individual decision comparisons, 3 samples per arm and show all 66 outcomes and errors. For each outcome and selected source-backed candidate, count correct and incorrect choices across three draws per arm. A repeatable improvement requires at least one agreed previously incorrect decision to become correct in at least 2 of 3 T draws and fewer than 2 of 3 C draws, with no agreed previously correct decision becoming wrong in at least 2 of 3 T draws while correct in at least 2 of 3 C draws. A repeatable regression stops the line. If neither occurs or independent readers disagree, report inconclusive. This is a screening rule for selected examples, not a quantitative estimate of product impact. Blind-read all eleven incoming records against all their candidate sets and source articles, including unchanged controls; report gaps. Register case ids and score mapping and historical top-ten replay before any send; send no paid calls until council review and preflight pass.
